      <h2 id="virt-creating-vm-by-cloning-pvcs-cli_virt-creating-vms-by-cloning-pvcs" class="group scroll-mt-20">Creating a VM from a PVC by using the CLI<a href="#virt-creating-vm-by-cloning-pvcs-cli_virt-creating-vms-by-cloning-pvcs" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can create a virtual machine (VM) by cloning the persistent volume claim (PVC) of an existing VM by using the command line.</p>
      <p>You can clone a PVC by using one of the following options:</p>
      <ul>
